Z||000000||2FAST4U||12-11-1999||04:54 AM||||According to the Ogre roller cams were available for 86 and up 4 cyl.<P>I have an 85 2M4 that has a roller cam. Is the Ogre wrong? Or do I a later engine. I bought the car used and don't know it's history.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||12-11-1999||05:16 AM||||<BR>I don't know what year was the first, but my '87 has a roller cam. I've read here at the forum that a roller cam can be installed in an older engine that did not originally have it. Maybe this is what happened with your car.||||reg||4
Z||000002||terryk||12-11-1999||12:08 PM||||Could be a model year crossover. GM does soft rolls on the cars. If there are 20 changes to be made from one MY to the next, they will start introducing the changes one at a time at the end of one MY and keep changing them until all of the new MY changes are in. It keeps the line running and limits the roll's impact to production.<P>Check your door label for the month of manufacturing. If it is June or later, it could be a crossover model. <P>I have an 86 Ciera GT with a slanted rear window which was technically not available until 87. You could have an 85-86 crossover car. Just makes parts a bit more challenging!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tim||12-11-1999||02:58 PM||||I understand 1985 2.5 had roller cam.  First Year.||||reg||1
